cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Epsilon-Hollow (Seal OS): an operating system whose state is topology on the 2-sphere"
abstract: >-
  A bare-metal x86_64 microkernel research operating system, written
  Rust-first as a no_std kernel with minimal assembly (AP trampoline,
  CPU idle). No POSIX, no libc. Operating-system state is represented as
  topology on the 2-sphere, and scheduling, memory, and device state are
  read through that geometric representation rather than through
  conventional table structures.
